ry Keywords: South Korea crypto, Polymarket users, DeFi regulation\n\n---\n\n# South Korea Opens First Polymarket Gambling Probe Targeting Domestic Users\n\nThe first-ever **Polymarket gambling probe** in South Korea is officially underway, signaling a major escalation in the nation's regulatory scrutiny of decentralized finance (DeFi). The Gangwon Provincial Police Agency has launched a criminal investigation targeting domestic users of the popular prediction market platform, acting on a formal request from the Korean National Police Agency (KNPA). This move puts the activities of countless traders under a legal microscope.\n\nThe investigation focuses on South Korean residents who placed bets on Polymarket, particularly surrounding the recent June 3 elections, which saw massive trading volumes. This action follows growing concerns from national regulators, including a formal review initiated in May by the Korea Communications Standards Commission (KCSC) to determine if the platform constitutes an illegal gambling operation under South Korean law.\n\n## South Korea's Regulatory Clampdown on Web3 Betting\n\nThe core of the issue lies in South Korea's tightly controlled monopoly on all forms of wagering. The government strictly limits legal betting to state-sanctioned channels, creating a direct conflict with the borderless nature of Web3 platforms like Polymarket."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":31,"aggregated":"META\n- SEO Title: Polymarket Gambling Probe: SK Investigates Users\n- Meta Description: South Korea has opened its first Polymarket gambling probe, targeting domestic users for illegal betting and escalating its crackdown on DeFi applications.\n- URL Slug: south-korea-polymarket-gambling-probe\n- Categories: Regulation, Latest News\n- Primary Keyword: Polymarket gambling probe\n- Secondary Keywords: South Korea crypto, Polymarket users, DeFi regulation\n\n---\n\n# South Korea Opens First Polymarket Gambling Probe Targeting Domestic Users\n\nThe first-ever **Polymarket gambling probe** in South Korea is officially underway, signaling a major escalation in the nation's regulatory scrutiny of decentralized finance (DeFi). The Gangwon Provincial Police Agency has launched a criminal investigation targeting domestic users of the popular prediction market platform, acting on a formal request from the Korean National Police Agency (KNPA). This move puts the activities of countless traders under a legal microscope.\n\nThe investigation focuses on South Korean residents who placed bets on Polymarket, particularly surrounding the recent June 3 elections, which saw massive trading volumes. This action follows growing concerns from national regulators, including a formal review initiated in May by the Korea Communications Standards Commission (KCSC) to determine if the platform constitutes an illegal gambling operation under South Korean law.\n\n## South Korea's Regulatory Clampdown on Web3 Betting\n\nThe core of the issue lies in South Korea's tightly controlled monopoly on all forms of wagering. The government strictly limits legal betting to state-sanctioned channels, creating a direct conflict with the borderless nature of Web3 platforms like Polymarket.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-publisher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780654884999},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /tmp/memecoinist-run-20260605-100719/article/with-image.md | head -n 20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gemini-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":3431,"output":53,"cacheRead":11024,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14508,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780654885003,"responseId":"KKMiavmoKNOD694Pl52y-Qg"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName"